<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Terminal Deck Native (Preview), signed with the hardened runtime. Only what it needs:

  * device.audio-input — voice input in Terminal Deck's screens (getUserMedia in the
    WKWebView). Under the hardened runtime the microphone is refused outright without
    it, before macOS even asks; Info.plist carries NSMicrophoneUsageDescription.
  * device.camera — a website in the in-app browser that asks for the camera (a video
    call, a photo taken in the page). Browser 27: without it WebKit refused every camera
    request; the tab asks the person first, then macOS asks once (NSCameraUsageDescription).

  * device.camera / automation.apple-events — a session may request these;
    macOS still requires the person's separate approval for each service.

  Deliberately absent, because nothing needs them:
  * cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory — WKWebView's JavaScript JIT runs in
    WebKit's own WebContent process, which Apple signs with its own entitlements.
  * cs.disable-library-validation — the app loads only system frameworks; SwiftTerm is
    linked in statically and its Metal shaders are a precompiled metallib (data).
  * App Intents and user notifications need no entitlement outside the App Sandbox,
    and this app is not sandboxed (it starts Terminal Deck as its engine).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
